{#
  Shelf guide, grouped by reader age.

  Two jobs. For parents it answers the question they actually arrive with —
  "is there anything here for a seven-year-old?" — before they drive over. For
  search it is the only place on the site where the terms people type ("picture
  books", "middle grade", "chapter books", "young adult") appear together in
  body copy under a heading, which the homepage previously had none of.
#}
<section id="shelves" class="shelf-guide">
    <h2>What's on the Shelves</h2>
    <p class="shelf-guide-intro">
        Every book in the store was read, argued over, or handed to us by a kid who
        wouldn't stop talking about it. Here's how the shelves break down.
    </p>

    <div class="shelf-guide-grid">
        <article class="shelf-band">
            <span class="shelf-band-age">Ages 0&ndash;3</span>
            <h3>Board Books</h3>
            <p>
                Built to survive being chewed, dropped, and read eleven times before
                breakfast. Touch-and-feel, first words, and the bedtime standbys that
                earn their wear.
            </p>
        </article>

        <article class="shelf-band">
            <span class="shelf-band-age">Ages 3&ndash;7</span>
            <h3>Picture Books</h3>
            <p>
                Our biggest section, and the one we're proudest of. Read-aloud favorites,
                laugh-out-loud stories, and the quiet ones that sneak up on you around
                the last page.
            </p>
        </article>

        <article class="shelf-band">
            <span class="shelf-band-age">Ages 5&ndash;8</span>
            <h3>Early Readers &amp; Chapter Books</h3>
            <p>
                The bridge years. Short chapters, big type, and series worth getting
                hooked on &mdash; because the book that turns a kid into a reader is
                usually the second one they finish, not the first.
            </p>
        </article>

        <article class="shelf-band">
            <span class="shelf-band-age">Ages 8&ndash;12</span>
            <h3>Middle Grade</h3>
            <p>
                Adventure, fantasy, mystery, and the realistic novels that help kids
                name what they're feeling. Ask us &mdash; this is the section where a
                good recommendation matters most.
            </p>
        </article>

        <article class="shelf-band">
            <span class="shelf-band-age">Ages 12+</span>
            <h3>Young Adult</h3>
            <p>
                Curated with actual teenagers in mind, not what adults think teenagers
                should be reading. We're happy to talk through content with parents who
                want to know what's inside.
            </p>
        </article>

        <article class="shelf-band">
            <span class="shelf-band-age">For grown-ups</span>
            <h3>Gifts &amp; Read-Alouds</h3>
            <p>
                Baby-shower gifts, birthday presents, and the family read-aloud pile.
                Tell us the kid and we'll find the book &mdash; it's the part of the job
                we like best.
            </p>
        </article>
    </div>

    <p class="shelf-guide-note">
        Looking for something specific? Call us at
        <a href="tel:{{ site.phoneRaw }}">{{ site.phone }}</a> &mdash; if it's not on the
        shelf, we can usually order it.
    </p>
</section>
